## Project Ideas for Major Project 1

1. Interactive Model Evaluation and Comparison Dashboard
   - Build a web-based dashboard using Streamlit or Dash.
   - Allow users to upload datasets, train models, and compare results interactively.
   - Include real-time visualizations for metrics like Dice, IoU, accuracy, and loss.

2. Explainable AI (XAI) for Predictions
   - Integrate Grad-CAM or SHAP to explain model predictions.
   - Provide heatmaps and feature importance for each prediction.
   - Add an interface to upload images and view explainable results.

3. Real-Time Video Polyp Detection
   - Extend the project to process colonoscopy videos in real-time.
   - Use OpenCV to process video frames and overlay bounding boxes for detected polyps.
   - Save annotated videos for further analysis.

4. Synthetic Dataset Generation
   - Use GANs or Diffusion Models to generate synthetic polyp images.
   - Add functionality to visualize and use synthetic datasets for training.
   - Compare model performance with and without synthetic data.

5. Automated Model Training Pipeline
   - Automate dataset preprocessing, model training, and evaluation.
   - Use MLflow or TensorBoard to log experiments and metrics.
   - Add a "Train Model" button in the dashboard to trigger the pipeline.

6. Polyp Severity Scoring System
   - Extend the model to classify polyps based on severity (e.g., benign, pre-cancerous, cancerous).
   - Provide severity scores along with predictions.
   - Add a feature to upload images/videos and get severity insights.

7. Crowdsourced Dataset Annotation Tool
   - Build a tool for collaborative annotation of polyp datasets.
   - Use Label Studio or create a custom annotation interface.
   - Allow users to upload unlabeled datasets and annotate them.

8. Knowledge Graph for Dataset and Model Insights
   - Build a knowledge graph to link datasets, models, metrics, and results.
   - Use Neo4j to create the graph database.
   - Visualize relationships in the dashboard to explore insights.

9. Open-Source Benchmarking Framework
   - Create a standardized framework for benchmarking polyp detection models.
   - Allow users to submit their own models and compare them against existing ones.
   - Display a leaderboard of model performance.

10. Curriculum Learning for Polyp Detection
    - Implement curriculum learning to train models by gradually increasing data complexity.
    - Start with easy samples and progressively introduce harder ones.
    - Compare model performance with and without curriculum learning.

11. RAG Chatbot for Dataset and Model Insights
    - Build a chatbot that uses Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to answer questions.
    - Allow users to query dataset statistics, model performance, and explainable predictions.
    - Use FAISS or Haystack for retrieval and Hugging Face Transformers for generation.
    - Integrate the chatbot into the dashboard or deploy it as a standalone app.